---
description: Angular components use external HTML templates, never inline template strings
globs: apps/web/**/*.ts
alwaysApply: false
---

# External Angular templates

Every `@Component` must use `templateUrl` pointing at a sibling `.html` file. Do not put markup in `template: \`...\`` or `template: '...'`.

```typescript
// ❌ BAD
@Component({
  selector: 'nb-mine-picker',
  template: `<button type="button">{{ t('lab.mine') }}</button>`,
})

// ✅ GOOD
@Component({
  selector: 'nb-mine-picker',
  templateUrl: './mine-picker.html',
})
```

```html
<!-- mine-picker.html -->
<button type="button">{{ t('lab.mine') }}</button>
```

- Name the file after the class file: `foo.ts` → `foo.html`.
- Keep class logic in `.ts`. Keep markup only in `.html`.
- Inline `host` / `styles` metadata is fine. Inline `template` is not, even for a single `<router-outlet />`.
